title: Immigration
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: immigration_timer <= 0 and dem_president = 1
on-arrival: immigration_timer = 8

= Immigration

Immigration is among the country's most emotionally charged issues. The Right uses it; the Left wants justice; most voters want order and humanity.

- @border_enforcement: Border security with legal pathways
- @path_to_citizenship: A path to citizenship
- @executive_action: Act by executive order
- @easy_discard

@border_enforcement
on-arrival: rural_dem += 3*(1-dissent); working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); minority_dem -= 1*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent += 5; maga_strength -= 1; month_actions += 1

We pair stricter enforcement with legal pathways.

@path_to_citizenship
on-arrival: minority_dem += 4*(1-dissent); young_dem += 2*(1-dissent); rural_dem -= 3*(1-dissent); working_dem -= 1*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent -= 4; maga_strength += 1.5; gop_enthusiasm += 0.3; month_actions += 1

Millions gain legal status, and the Right energizes.

@executive_action
on-arrival: minority_dem += 2*(1-dissent); rural_dem -= 2*(1-dissent); institutions -= 0.5; polarization += 1; month_actions += 1

Executive action helps some families, but invites courtroom battles.
